      "file": "packages/Webkul/Razorpay/src/Http/Controllers/RazorpayController.php",
      "anchor": "return \\$payment\\['amount'\\] === \\(int\\) round\\(\\$cart->base_grand_total \\* 100\\);",
      "also": [
        {
          "file": "packages/Webkul/Razorpay/src/Payment/RazorpayPayment.php",
          "anchor": "'amount' => \\(int\\) \\(\\$cart->base_grand_total \\* 100\\),"
        }
      ],
      "note": "paymentCoversCart compares the captured amount with round(total * 100), but the Razorpay order is created with (int)(total * 100), which truncates. For totals like 19.99 the float product is 1998.99..., so the order asks for 1998 paise and the check expects 1999: the buyer is charged, the check refuses the payment and no order is placed."
    }
